---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const site = 'https://txttocsv.com';
const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  mainEntity: {
    '@type': 'Person',
    name: 'Saad Zaman',
    url: `${site}/about`,
    image: `${site}/saad-zaman.webp`,
    email: 'info@txttocsv.com',
    sameAs: ['https://x.com/saad7038'],
  },
};
---
<Base
  title="About txttocsv: Who Builds and Maintains This Tool"
  description="txttocsv is a free, privacy-first converter for text and CSV files. Learn who builds it, why it exists, and how conversions are kept accurate and local."
  schema={schema}
>
  <article class="wrap section article">
    <nav class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <span>About</span></nav>
    <h1>About txttocsv</h1>
    <p class="lead">A small, focused tool that does one job well: converting between plain text and CSV without mangling your data.</p>

    <h2>Why this exists</h2>
    <p>
      Most text-to-CSV conversions fail on the same small things. A value with a comma splits a row.
      A tab file gets read as commas. Accented characters turn to symbols in Excel. Many online
      converters also upload your file to a server, which is a problem when the data is not yours to share.
      txttocsv was built to fix all of that: correct quoting, reliable delimiter handling, and processing
      that happens entirely in your browser.
    </p>

    <h2>Who builds it</h2>
    <div class="byline" style="margin-bottom:1rem">
      <img src="/saad-zaman.webp" alt="Saad Zaman" width="64" height="64" style="width:64px;height:64px" />
      <div>
        <strong>Saad Zaman</strong><br />
        <a href="https://x.com/saad7038" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">@saad7038 on X</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>
      This site is built and maintained by Saad Zaman, a developer who works with data exports and
      import pipelines. The converter and every guide on the site come from hands-on use of these
      formats and the everyday problems they cause, not from rewritten documentation. When a guide
      says a method drops leading zeros or garbles encoding, it is because that happened on a real file.
    </p>

    <h2>How we keep it accurate</h2>
    <p>
      Every method described in a guide is tested before it is published. Conversion behaviour follows
      the CSV specification, RFC 4180, so results match what Excel, Google Sheets, pandas and databases
      expect. Our full editorial approach is on the <a href="/methodology">editorial policy</a> page.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions, corrections or feature requests are welcome at
      <a href="mailto:info@txttocsv.com">info@txttocsv.com</a>, or through the
      <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
